{{also|Appendix:Variations of "time"}}
==English==
{{wp}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|tyme||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|id=main|:inh|enm:tyme|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|tyme}}, {{m|enm|time}}, from {{inh|en|ang|tīma|t=time, period, space of time, season, lifetime, fixed time, favorable time, opportunity}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*tīmō}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*tīmô||time}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*déh₂imō}}, from {{m+|ine-pro|*deh₂y-|*deh₂-i-|to divide}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*deh₂-}}. Related to {{m|en|tide}}. Not related to {{noncog|la|tempus}}. Distant {{dbt|nocap=1|en|demon//daemon|daimon}} (or {{pwd|nocap=1|en|}}, if the Greek and Germanic words were suffixed independently).
{{col-top|2|cog}}
* {{cog|sco|tym}}, {{m|sco|tyme||time}}
* {{cog|gsw|Zimen}}, {{m|gsw|Zimmän|Zīmmän|time, time of the year, opportune time, opportunity}}
* {{cog|da|time||hour, lesson}}
* {{cog|ovd|taime||hour}}
* {{cog|fo|tími||hour, lesson, time}}
* {{cog|is|tími||time, season}}
* {{cog|no|time||lesson, hour}}
* {{cog|sv|timma}}, {{m|sv|timme||hour}}.
{{col-bottom}}

