#: {{ux|en|Your car runs three '''times''' faster than mine.}}
#: {{ux|en|That is four '''times''' as heavy as this.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1980
|author=James Chan
|editors=C. K. Leung; Norton Ginsburg
|chapter=Modern Manufacturing Industries in Kuangtung
|title=China: Urbanization and National Development
|url=https://archive.org/details/chinaurbanizatio0000unse/
|ISBN=0-89065-103-5
|LCCN=80-29142
|OCLC=7175420
|page=220
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/chinaurbanizatio0000unse/page/220/
|text=Canton is the regional primate city of Kuangtung. Its population of three million is ten '''times''' that of the second largest city, Shant'ou.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Spin Off|year=2026|volume=L|number=1|page=16|title=Yagaa: Reviving Sericulture in Southern Mexico|author=Elise Young
|text=A mature silkworm is an impressive 2¾ inches (70 mm) long and eats 50,000 '''times''' its mature body weight over the course of its development.}}
# {{lb|en|music|uncountable}} The [[measured]] [[duration]] of [[sound]]s.
#: {{q|dated}} {{coi|en|dance '''time'''; &nbsp; march '''time'''}} {{q|see usage notes}}
## {{senseid|en|tempo}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} {{1|tempo}}; a measured rate of movement.
##: {{ux|en|The musician keeps good '''time'''.}}
##* {{RQ:Beaumont Fletcher Comedies and Tragedies|The False One|1|2||some few lines set unto a solemn '''time'''}}
## {{senseid|en|meter}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[rhythmical|Rhythmical]] [[division]], [[meter]].
##: {{ux|en|common or triple '''time'''; &nbsp; [['''time''' signature]]}}
