===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|en|inh-en-enm-til}}
From {{inh|en|enm|til}}, from [[w:Northumbrian Old English|Northern]] {{inh|en|ang|til}}, from or akin to {{der|en|non|til|t=to, till}}; both from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*til|t=to, toward}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*tilą|t=planned point in time}}.<ref>Kroonen, Guus. 2013. Etymological Dictionary of Proto-Germanic</ref><ref> {{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|till}}</ref> Not a contraction of {{m|en|until}}; rather, ''until'' comes from ''till'' with the prefix {{m|en|un-|t=against; toward; up to}} also found in {{m|en|unto}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|til|t=to, till}}, {{cog|da|til|t=to}}, {{cog|sv|till|t=to, till}}, {{cog|is|til|t=to, till}}. Also related to {{cog|ang|til|t=good}}, {{cog|de|Ziel|t=goal}}, {{cog|got|𐍄𐌹𐌻|t=something fitting or suitable}}.

====Alternative forms====
