|passage=Similar sentiments will recur to everyone familiar with his writings all through them '''till''' the very end.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1946|month=May and June|author=G. A. Sekon|title=L.B.S.C.R. West Coast Section—3|journal=Railway Magazine|page=148|text=The line was authorised on June 23, 1864, but not opened '''till''' July 11, 1881.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en| date=2019-3-14| author=Ramzy Baroud| journal=Ma'an News| url=https://www.maannews.com/Content.aspx?id=782867| title=Chasing mirages: What are Palestinians doing to combat ‘Deal of the Century’?| passage=While the PA has not always seen eye-to-eye with US foreign policy, its survival remained, '''till''' recently, a top American priority.| accessdate=15 July 2019| archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190330063151/http://www.maannews.com/Content.aspx?ID=782867| archivedate=30 March 2019}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=4 December 2024|author=|title=This place in NZ has such a long name that most people can't pronounce it |journal={{w|Times of India}}|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/travel/destinations/this-place-in-nz-has-such-a-long-name-that-most-people-cant-pronounce-it/articleshow/115940825.cms|text=If you thought Wytrzyszczka was a mouthful, wait '''till''' you try saying [[Taumatawhakatangihangakoauauotamateaturipukakapikimaungahoronukupokaiwhenuakitanatahu]].|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241204105653/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/travel/destinations/this-place-in-nz-has-such-a-long-name-that-most-people-cant-pronounce-it/articleshow/115940825.cms}}
# [[before|Before]] (a certain time or event).
#: {{ux|en|It's twenty '''till''' two. (1:40)}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1880|author=A. T. Fullerton|title=Fever|journal=Littell's Living Age|volume=147|page=578|text=Is that the town-clock striking? / I think that it is to-night / My fever will reach its crisis, / There are long hours yet '''till''' light.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|or|dialectal}} [[to|To]], [[up to]] (physically).
