#* {{quote-book|en|title=Popular Ballads and Songs| editor=Robert Jameson| chapter=Lord Wa'Yates and Auld Ingram| volume=2| year=1806| passage=And '''till''' the kirk she wadna gae,&nbsp;/ nor '''till''''t she wadna ride,&nbsp;/ '''Till''' four-and-twenty men she gat her before,&nbsp;/ And twenty on ilka side}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Minstrelsy of the Scottish Border| editor=w:Walter Scott| chapter=The Outlaw Murray| year=1838| passage=For a king to gang an outlaw '''till'''&nbsp;/ Is beneath his state and his dignitie.}}
