## A [[gratuity]]; a small [[amount]] of money left for a [[bartender]], [[waiter]], [[taxi driver]] or other service worker as a [[token]] of appreciation, often calculated as a percentage of the bill. {{defdate|from mid-18th c.}}
##: {{ux|en|Workers in the American [[service industry]] usually depend on '''tips''' to even make [[minimum wage]].}}
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1964|author=w:Ernest Hemingway|title=w:A Moveable Feast|page=156
|passage=“Did you tip him enough to do any good? They only work for '''tips'''.”<br>“I didn’t know that,” I said. “I thought the hotel paid them something on the side.”<br>“I mean they will only do something for you for a substantial '''tip'''. Most of them are rotten clean through.”}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 December 14|author=David Turner|title=The Edwardian Christmas getaway...|journal=RAIL|issue=972|page=35|text='''Tips''' were an important part of porters' income, and at Christmas passengers felt there was extra pressure to give them - despite some perceiving the level of service to be poor.}}
## {{lb|en|dated}} A gratuity given to someone who voluntarily provides assistance.
##* {{RQ:Stoker Dracula|||A half crown '''tip''' put the deputy's knowledge at my disposal, and I learned that Mr. Bloxam [...] had left for his work at five o'clock that morning.}} 
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1899|author=E. Nesbit|title=[[s:The Story of the Treasure Seekers/Chapter 10|The Story of the Treasure Seekers]]|passage=So Lord Tottenham said, "Well, I'm much obliged any way. And now I come to look at you—of course, you're not young ruffians, but gentlemen's sons, eh? Still, you won't be above taking a '''tip''' from an old boy—I wasn't when I was your age," and he pulled out half a sovereign.}}
## {{lb|en|dated}} A small monetary gift given to a child from an older relative or family friend.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1955|author=C. S. Lewis|title=The Magician’s Nephew|text=“I hope,” said Uncle Andrew presently in a very high and mighty voice, just as if he were a perfect Uncle who had just given one a handsome '''tip''' and some good advice}}

