===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|mathematics}} A [[mathematical]] [[statement]] of some [[importance]] that has been [[prove]]n to be [[true]]. Minor theorems are often called ''[[proposition]]s''. Theorems which are not very interesting in themselves but are an [[essential]] part of a bigger theorem's [[proof]] are called ''[[lemma]]s''.
# {{lb|en|mathematics|colloquial|nonstandard}} A [[mathematical]] [[statement]] that is [[expected]] to be [[true]].
#: {{ux|en|[[w:Fermat's Last Theorem|Fermat's Last '''Theorem''']] was known thus long before it was proved in the 1990s.}}
# {{lb|en|logic}} A [[syntactically]] correct [[expression]] that is [[deducible]] from the given [[axioms]] of a [[deductive]] [[system]].

