===Noun===
[[File:Epidauros Ancient Theatre.jpg|thumb|the ancient '''theater''' (1) of Epidaurus]]
{{en-noun|~}} {{tlb|en|American spelling}}

# {{sid|en|Q11635}}{{lb|en|countable}} A place or [[building]], consisting of a [[stage]] and seating, in which an [[audience]] gathers to watch [[play]]s, musical performances, public ceremonies, and so on.
#: {{syn|en|playhouse}}
# A region where a particular action takes place; a specific field of action, usually with reference to war.
#: {{ux|en|His grandfather was in the Pacific '''theater''' during the war.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=w:Colson Whitehead|title=w:The Nickel Boys|publisher=Fleet|page=69|passage=Percy had been too big for the town since he got back from the war. He served in the Pacific '''theater''', behind the lines keeping up the supply chain.}}
# A [[lecture theatre]].
# {{lb|en|medicine}} An [[operating theatre]] or locale for human experimentation.
#: {{ux|en|This man is about to die, get him into '''theater''' at once!}}
# {{lb|en|US}} A [[cinema]].
#: {{ux|en|We sat in the back row of the '''theater''' and threw popcorn at the screen.}}
# Drama or performance as a profession or art form.
#: {{syn|en|fabulous invalid}}
#: {{ux|en|I worked in '''theater''' for twenty-five years.}}
# Any place rising by steps like the seats of a theater.
# {{lb|en|figurative|derogatory|often following a noun used attributively}} A conspicuous but unproductive display of action.
#: {{uxi|en|The Senate confirmation hearings were just '''theater'''.}}
#: {{uxi|en|[[security theater|security '''theater''']]; [[hygiene theater|hygiene '''theater''']]}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Andrew Rens|url=https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=2051175|journal=Suffolk Transnational Law Review|volume=35|year=2012|title=Enforcement Theater: The Enforcement Agenda and the Institutionalization of Enforcement Theater in the Anti-Counterfeiting Trade Agreement|passage=ACTA proponents rely on claims of a growing piracy and counterfeiting threat. In the absence of credible evidence of the threat or that the measures in ACTA will reduce the threat, ACTA is no more than enforcement '''theater'''.}}

====Usage notes====
* The spelling {{m|en|theatre}} is the main spelling in British, Canadian, Australian and New Zealand English, with {{m|en||theater}} being rare.
* In United States English, {{m|en||theater}} accounts for about 80 percent of usage in the major corpus of usage, [[COCA]].
* Some Americans may use the two spellings to differentiate between the location {{m|en||theater}} and the art-form {{m|en||theatre}}. Alternatively, some people use {{m|en||theatre}} for things relating to live performances (and sometimes films and cinemas) like musical ''theatre'', with {{m|en||theater}} being used for other uses (such as a ''theater of war'').

